# telegram.env — OPTIONAL Telegram alert sink for the VPS brain (fleetctl
# notify(), docs/FLEET-BRAIN.md §4 Q4). PLACEHOLDERS ONLY — never put real
# values in this file; never commit real values anywhere.
#
# Seed on the VPS as:
#   install -m 600 /dev/null /etc/grok-fleet/telegram.env
#   $EDITOR /etc/grok-fleet/telegram.env    # fill both vars below
#
# Behavior (fleetctl notify()): every alert is written to the journal/stderr
# ALWAYS. When this file exists, fleetctl sources BOTH variables in a subshell
# (token never echoed) and POSTs to the Telegram Bot API sendMessage
# (10s timeout, text prefixed "[grok-fleet/<level>]"). Absent file, empty vars,
# or no curl => journal-only, no error. vps/install-vps.sh never seeds this
# file; the note in its summary points here.

TELEGRAM_BOT_TOKEN="0000000000:AAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAA"
TELEGRAM_CHAT_ID="-1000000000000"
